     "table_container_copy_558282354": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "bruno.jaques@macnicadhw.com.br",
      "text": "<table cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n<tbody><tr><td width=\"20%\" style=\"width:123px;\"><b>TQMa53-AA</b></td>\n<td><ul>\n<li>TQMa53, i.MX537 / 800 MHz, 4 GB e-MMC flash, 512 MB DDR3, 64 kbit EEPROM, -25°C …+85°C</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr><tr><td width=\"25%\" style=\"width:123px;\"><b>STKa53-AA</b></td>\n<td><ul>\n<li>STKa53 (Eval Kit) with TQMa53-AA, i.MX537 / 800 MHz, 512 MB DDR3, 4 GB e-MMC flash, 64 kbit EEPROM, 1x RS232, 1x RS485 , 2 x CAN 2.0B separated, 3x USB 2.0 HOST, 1x USB 2.0 OTG, 2x ETH 10/100, CRT, 2x LVDS, Line Out, Mono Mic In, Line In, RTC, Temperature sensor, Reset button, SD interface, Power Supply, 2 GB SD card, Z-Modem cable, USB cable, DVI-VGA adapter, DVI-HDMI adapter</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr><tr><td style=\"width:123px;\"><b>Starter kit STKa53 set</b></td>\n<td><ul>\n<li>The core of the STKa53 set is the TQMa53 with the i.MX53 CPU from Freescale. With the preconfigured starter kit you can start immediately with the development of your application in order to achieve a fast time-to-market. To develop your own hardware you can use the certified and qualified circuit components of the starter kit in your own designs. A large accessory kit enables the connection of commercial monitors. Different display solutions for a direct connection to LVDS / TTL are available upon request.</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr></tbody></table>",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Aug 31 2026 23:27:54 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "macnicaglobal2/components/content/table",
      "textIsRich": "true",
